    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25840" root="ضعف" body-key="D">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضعفهُ</span></b>  <i>He,</i> (God, Msb, or another, S,) or
<i>it,</i> (disease, TA,) <i>rendered him</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَعِيف</span> [i. e. <i>weak,</i>
&amp;c.]; (S, O, Msb, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضعّفهُ</span></b> . (L, TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَضْعَفَ</span>, said of a man, <i>He became one
whose beast was weak.</i> (S, O, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See also 3,
first sentence, and last two sentences.

